             on the Anthropic Messages API (beta path, for the server-side refusal fallback) with the
            official C# SDK and the organization's own key. One non-streaming request per pre-review:


system: the store's reviewer prompt and the catalog rules, the second block marked for prompt caching;

user: the submission as escaped data, then each screenshot (base64 JPEG) after its text label;

adaptive thinking (the default; never disabled), the effort of , no
            sampling parameters, no prefill;

the report as structured output (output_config.format with );

fallbacks: "default" with the server-side-fallback-2026-07-01 beta on models that support it.

            The stop reason is checked before the content is read, and only text blocks are read. Errors become a
            ; the provider's answer and the key are never logged or passed on.

