The job: runs one AI pre-review. Steps on the activity hub:
submission.read: reads the store record live (content and readiness check for the App Store and Google Play, the current content for the Microsoft Store) and storeasy's records (saved answers, in-app products, past rejections) into a ;
screenshots.load: downloads and scales down the chosen screenshots;
ai.review: asks with the organization's key and saves the report, the usage and the cost estimate.
Every failure is saved on the pre-review with its message key before the job fails, so the history shows why. Nothing is written to a store. The audit entry keeps the model, the verdict, the counts, the tokens and the cost; no app content and never the key.

